{"description":"WI-A of the telemetry prerequisite for sto:compliance-telemetry (M5), per adr:038-telemetry-capture and spec:telemetry-capture:1. Provide the emit side: the `eka telemetry emit` command appending one append-only JSONL record to docs/telemetry/\u003csessionId\u003e.jsonl with a prevHash chain, the client-supplied sessionId semantics (no fabrication), the opt-in auto-emit on the write and gate paths, the read-only read path, the capture transport skip-list entry, and the source-only attachment round-trip. No store-schema, corpus, envelope or standard change.","acceptanceCriteria":"- `eka telemetry emit --event \u003ckind\u003e --session \u003cid\u003e [--subject] [--constraint] [--gate] [--reason]` appends exactly one JSONL line to docs/telemetry/\u003cid\u003e.jsonl; the file is never rewritten; prevHash validates the chain (a mismatch is a deterministic error).\n- With no --session, the record is written with sessionId \"\" and sessionSource \"unattributed\"; two runs with no session produce two unattributed records and no synthesized id.\n- Auto-emit (only when a session id is present): eka transition refusal and eka verify fail produce a gate-refusal with the correct gate and reason; eka publish success produces first-write then write; eka verify pass produces gate-pass\n- Reads never write: eka get / eka context change neither the telemetry files nor the store.\n- docs/telemetry/\u003cid\u003e.jsonl appears as an attachment in an EmitSource/LoadSnapshot round-trip with a repo-relative id and a matching digest.\n- `telemetry` is in captureTransportDirs: a telemetry file name never affects eka capture classification.\n- gofmt/vet/build/test green; deterministic output; no new go.mod dependency."}